From dd402d478798f4af8ec9d00853221f9dcec15932 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TriSenseINSLIB <noreply@voltinolabs.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Attitude without Euler singularities: mag azimuth, TRIAD
 alignment, heading axis

ahrs_fuse_mag: heading measured as the azimuth of the field in the n-frame,
h_n = R_b_to_n * mag_b, z = wrap(declination - atan2(h_E, h_N)), H = -e_z on
the n-frame attitude error (same H as before, no Euler angles). Skipped only
where the horizontal field vanishes (magnetic pole), not near pitch +-90.

nav_suite: the magnetometer AHRS starts from a TRIAD attitude (gravity +
field, new ahrs_triad_attitude / ahrs_set_initial_attitude) instead of
leveling roll/pitch + de-tilted heading + ins_quat_from_rpy. Without a
magnetometer: tilt from gravity, heading 0, as before.

ins: new ins_options_t.heading_axis_b (default body x = ZYX yaw, unchanged
behaviour). ins_fuse_yaw, the automotive course yaw and the auto-init yaw
use the azimuth of that axis and skip only while it is vertical.
